## Phase 20: Fix Equity-Based Drawdown Logic

Identified why new entries were blocked incorrectly on March 4th.

- **The Problem**: The bot was calculating drawdown based on **Available Capital**. When a 15% position was opened, the available capital dropped from $100 to $85, which the bot interpreted as a **15% Loss** (Maximum Drawdown), even though no money was actually lost yet.
- **The Fix**: I updated the engine to calculate drawdown based on **Account Equity** (Available Balance + Open Position Sizes).
- **Benefit**: Opening large positions will no longer trigger the "Safety Halt" unless the positions actually start losing money. 15% conviction trades will now allow subsequent trades to fire as long as they fit within the exposure limits.

The bot is now correctly distinguishing between **Capital Allocation** and **Realized Losses**.

